    "audience": "agents",
    "title": "The arras amendment window",
    "source_slug": "arras_contract_en",
    "source_article": "property-contracts.txt",
    "post_text": "There's a window built into every arras that most foreign buyers never use. The draft arrives a couple of days before signing precisely so someone can request amendments.\n\nIf you sell to foreign buyers, that window is where the deal is really made, because this contract decides everything that follows.\n\nWorth knowing how the document is usually born, too. Most agencies work from a standard template, amended with the exact details of the property as they appear on the Nota Simple, plus the clauses that safeguard both parties. Templates are fine, but they're also why line by line checking matters, because a template doesn't know about this seller's furniture or that buyer's mortgage.\n\nSo what should be inside? An accurate description of the property, address, size and layout. The price. A completion date, usually two to three months out, which has to leave enough time for the buyer's documentation and any mortgage. The penalties if either side pulls out. And then the specifics, meaning furniture the sellers leave, repairs they agreed to fund, whether appliances are included, whether water and electricity will be switched on. If it isn't written here, it was never agreed.\n\nThe stakes are real on both sides. Once signed, a buyer who withdraws loses the 10 percent deposit, and a seller who withdraws pays double. That's why the draft goes out a couple of days early, so the buyer or their representative can read it and push back.\n\nTwo more habits worth building. The 10 percent sometimes goes straight to the owners, which is common, but a safeguarded account at a financial institution is the safer route, so raise it. And on a new build, add completion date clauses of their own, plus a look at the bank guarantee standing behind the staged payments.\n\nSend the draft to your buyer the day it lands, with one line: read this now, not at the table.\n\n#SpainProperty #BuyingInSpain #RealEstateSpain",
    "image_url": "/photos/pool_dusk.jpg"
